{
  "_about": "Order 264.8: which datasheet fact SETTLES that a standard's Part (a division whose own scope limits it to one construction) applies to this equipment. A family is named by the words a Part's scope uses for it (every word of one `scope_words` entry is in the Part's construction phrase) and is settled by a stated fact: a fact whose label and value match one of `patterns` (and, when `roles` is not null, whose field is one of those roles; a MATERIAL family is settled by the shell or the heads only: a tube, a seal or a lining is not the vessel). Only 'applies' is ever decided from here; a Part is never excluded from here. DRAFT: a client discipline engineer approves the lists before they are relied on. No standard and no Part is named.",
